Appendix D — The Adversary Capability Lattice and Its Consequences

D.1 Capability Definitions

Adversary A (reporting-integrity). For every observation o_j with host-mediated provenance, \mathcal{A} may replace o_j(X) by any element of \Omega_j. This is a capability over the transport of observations, not over the forgery of signatures.

Adversary \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{rel}} (relay). \mathcal{A} can route an attestation conversation to a genuine component c' at p' \neq p while the verifier believes it addresses c at p.

Adversary \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{int}} (channel-integrity). \mathcal{A} can influence the protected link: reorder protected TLPs undetected, cause tag aliasing after completion timeout, or cause stale data to be consumed after incomplete flush or re-keying.

D.2 Ordering

\mathbb{A} \prec \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{rel}}, \qquad \mathbb{A} \prec \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{int}},

while \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{rel}} and \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{int}} are incomparable. Relay corrupts referential integrity; channel-integrity corruption preserves reference while breaking contextual integrity. No scalar “attack resistance” is well defined.

D.3 Proposition 1 and the Corrected Counterexample

Proposition 1 states that if V is \kappa_2-sound then V is \kappa_1-sound for \kappa_1 \preceq \kappa_2, and the converse fails.

Corrected converse counterexample. A verifier that validates a hardware-rooted, nonce-bound channel identifier is \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{rel}}-sound for the endpoint claim: the relay cannot forward or replay the transcript because the identifier is bound to the endpoint and to the challenge nonce. The same verifier remains vulnerable to \mathbb{B}_{\mathrm{int}} if link ordering is not enforced, because the adversary can reorder protected TLPs without triggering detection. The two soundness properties are independent.

The qualification “hardware-rooted, nonce-bound” is essential. A relay can forward a transcript bearing an unbound identifier, or replay a previously observed one. Binding to endpoint and nonce is what defeats forwarding.

