Appendix F — Items That Must Remain Unknown

The framework requires the following to be recorded as unknown until primary-source confirmation is available. Promoting any of them to a definite value is a category error.

1. PDI claim semantics. Signer, scope, and freshness are not in the public schema. B_{3b} is “to be tested”.
2. TDISP availability on the tested GPU. Recorded per platform; not assumed.
3. PPCIE v2.x PDI enforcement. Whether the C++ verifier enforces PDI presence and validation is not documented publicly.
4. BMC trustworthiness on the tested platform. Recorded, not assumed. Whether the BMC is a hardware root is platform-dependent.
5. m_{9613} on the tested link. Currently \mathsf{U} on all known shipping platforms. The value becomes \mathsf{E} only when the revised TDISP specification ships and is validated on the specific link.
6. \rho(\ell) on the tested platform. Recorded. \rho = 1 places the link in the residual stratum unless a validated switch mitigation is documented for that specific switch.
7. IDE Escort support on both endpoints. A pair property; recorded per link, not per component.
8. TDISP normative text. Members-only; claims in this framework rely on secondary sources and must be confirmed against the normative text before any result is presented as depending on it.
9. A concrete link-history pair for Proposition 4. Not constructed. Indeterminacy is the strongest claim available.
10. DICE Concise Evidence Binding for SPDM. Listed but not read in full. Its content may affect the L_1 classification.

